    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini-session\n\n### Description\n\nHello, \r\n\r\nSo this is a pretty straightforward problem. When `mini-sessions` starts it takes a snapshot of the sessions directory in the setup. If afterwards you start another neovim instance, delete a session, then go back to the original instance you'll still see the deleted session show up with `require(\"mini.sessions\").select()`. Or if you add a session, it won't be visible in the other instance. A simple solution would be to have the detected sessions refreshed before every operation. \n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.9.0-dev-678+g922075530\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOpen 2 Neovim instances, delete a session in one and use `require(\"mini.sessions\").select()` in the other.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nList of sessions not synchronized across instances.",
