        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Admittedly it doesn't have a significant effect on usability, but I've caught myself several times opening sessions I've deleted. It's a marginal improvement, but I think it would take a marginal change to the code, wouldn't it? We'd run `detect_sessions` at the beginning of `write`,`delete`, and `select`.\r\n\r\nBut again, I like mini because of it's simplicity if you think it's giving up too much for too little that's fair.",
